jr-title = And you always know why it spoke.
jr-lede = Everything it does is written down: what it heard, what it did, and the reason behind every word it said on its own. Open the journal and follow the thread.
jr-clip = The journal in Nestor’s admin: a new event arrives, then a story opens with its reasons.
jr-dev-title = The journal is the source of truth.
jr-dev-text = Every turn, tool call, task, memory change, unprompted message and policy decision is an event in an append-only log, in one SQLite file. The admin, durable tasks and replay are all read from it — so “why did it speak to me?” always has an answer.
jr-dev-clip = Filtering the journal by person and channel in the admin.
